  "reasoning": "The defendants, as the actual controller and legal representative/miner of the coal mine, neglected safety management, allowed illegal production, leading to a fatal mine collapse that killed four workers. This constitutes a major responsibility accident under Article 133 of the Criminal Law (重大责任事故罪). After the accident they concealed it and failed to report it to authorities, which is punishable as the crime of failing to report an accident under Article 338 (未报告事故罪). Both offenses are applicable.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]重大责任事故罪;未报告事故罪<eoa>"
}
